{"chunk_id": "9df2d8e78fb4", "text": "This section first recounts Vishnu\u2019s descent in the form of a colossal boar to the netherworld, where he confronts thousands of Daityas. Though the demons surround and try to overpower him, they fail; his terrifying roars shake the cosmos, paralyzing the Danavas and striking fear even among the gods. Vishnu slaughters the demons and is praised as the eternal, supreme being\u2014Sanatana, Padmanabha, the source and lord of all creation. The narrative then shifts to a philosophical dialogue: Yudhishthira asks Bhishma about the yoga that leads to liberation. Bhishma introduces an ancient teaching in which a disciple questions his guru about the origin of beings, the nature of reality, and the meaning of Vedic teachings, beginning a discourse on Adhyatma and the supreme nature of Vasudeva.\nVishnu as the cosmic Boar destroys the Danavas, after which a dialogue begins on the supreme yoga and Vasudeva as the ultimate reality.\nThemes: divine intervention, Vishnu Varaha, cosmic power, yoga and emancipation, metaphysics of Vasudeva", "vector": [-0.00045233970740810037, -0.02140631154179573, -0.0069780051708221436, 0.03075909987092018, -0.028257926926016808, 0.010929325595498085, -0.04502110183238983, -0.022736720740795135, -0.02195177972316742, -0.014142267405986786, -7.249700138345361e-05, 0.023508360609412193, 0.001145816408097744, -0.0016538669588044286, 0.0017311971168965101, 0.000977852032519877, 0.038794782012701035, -0.01951712742447853, 0.0336327850818634, -0.0003168041002936661, -0.004463528282940388, -0.004323835484683514, -0.007749643176794052, 0.01713569276034832, -0.014740952290594578, 0.017481599003076553, 0.03307401388883591, -0.019557040184736252, 0.009126618504524231, -0.004929172340780497, -0.008960316888988018, 0.0023448490537703037, 0.013603450730443, 0.002933555981144309, -0.009126618504524231, 0.012559078633785248, 0.007836120203137398, 0.004842695314437151, 0.01479416899383068, -0.005627637729048729, 0.010051